-- Row il-80. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: the instruments, the printed texts, the instructions and the table rows that the two items read, item I1 and item I2, and the commencements as the pages print them.
-- Tests of the controls are in df80-tests-controls.l4, tests that pin the readings are in df80-tests-readings.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose (three: one for I1, two for I2) are in df80-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[shNNN-pPPP]` lines quote the Hebrew printed on the deposited image of Sefer HaChukim (SH) issue NNN, printed page PPP (registers/source-bundle/pages/); `ext:[nv10-pPPP]` lines quote the deposited image of the New Version of the Civil Wrongs Ordinance, printed page PPP. They are official instruments.
-- Every Hebrew string typed below is a stretch of the ext: line above it (or of a src: line), and tools/hebcheck.py checks that each Hebrew run of this module is in the excerpt or on an ext: line.
-- A word broken by a hyphen at the end of a printed line is typed whole. A dash is typed as the en dash. Gershayim and geresh are typed as the Hebrew marks.
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md.

§ `References`

